# SecuBox-Deb :: secubox-ytsas :: host nft egress scope
# CyberMind — https://cybermind.fr
#
# Scopes the ytsas LXC's egress. FORWARD/OUTPUT are policy-accept repo-wide
# (see CLAUDE.md nftables rules) — no blanket DROP is introduced here. yt-dlp
# needs broad HTTPS egress to reach YouTube and every yt-dlp-supported site, so
# this is an explicit visibility tap (LOG on new connections) on the LXC's
# veth, not an allow/deny gate.
#
# Own, fully self-contained table + base chain (mirrors the torrent /
# secubox-p2p egress drop-ins): loads independently of any other table already
# present on the board, and never issues a global ruleset reset.
#
# Matches the exact veth pair name pinned by install-lxc.sh
# (`lxc.net.0.veth.pair = veth-ytsas0`) — LXC otherwise assigns a random
# vethXXXXXX name on every start, which a static nft rule can't target.
#
# Loaded by /etc/nftables.conf via `include "/etc/nftables.d/*.nft"`. Shipped
# as zz-ytsas-egress.nft at install time so it sorts after any table-creator
# base file, per repo convention (feedback_nft_layered_dropins_persistence).
table inet secubox_ytsas {
    chain forward_ytsas {
        type filter hook forward priority 0; policy accept;
        iifname "veth-ytsas0" ct state new log prefix "[SECUBOX-YTSAS] " level info
    }
}
